# EnterprisePulse Web

React 19 + Vite + TypeScript client for the EnterprisePulse ERP. The API lives in a separate repository
(`enterprise-pulse-api`); this app talks to it **only** through the generated client in `src/api/generated`.

## Stack

TanStack Router (file-based, typed) · TanStack Query · TanStack Table v8 · shadcn/ui (radix) + Tailwind 4 ·
React Hook Form + zod 3 · i18next (tr, en) · Zustand (session store) · Orval (OpenAPI → hooks) · socket.io-client · Vitest · Playwright.

## Layout

```
src/
  api/http.ts              axios instance (token, company/branch headers, refresh on 401) = Orval mutator
  api/generated/           Orval output – NEVER edit by hand, run `pnpm api:generate`
  app/                     providers, router, query client, layout (sidebar, header, switchers)
  routes/                  file routes only: guards (`beforeLoad`) + render a feature page
  features/<module>/       pages, dialogs and hooks of one business module
  shared/ui/               shadcn primitives (generated, keep close to upstream)
  shared/components/       app-level building blocks: DataTable, PageHeader, ConfirmDialog, SimpleFormDialog, badges
  shared/lib/              utils, format, validation helpers, query helpers
  i18n/locales/{tr,en}.json
```

## Rules that always apply

- Code and identifiers in **English**; every user-visible string goes through `t('...')` with keys in **both** `tr.json` and `en.json`. Turkish is the default language.
- Imports across folders use the `@/` alias.
- Route files stay tiny; page logic lives in `src/features/<module>/`.
- Server state = TanStack Query via generated hooks. Client state = local `useState` or Zustand (only session/company/branch). No server data in Zustand.
- Hide what the user cannot do (`<Can permission>` / `usePermission()`), and guard routes with `beforeLoad: requirePermission('module:read')`. The API is still the source of truth.
- Money mutations (payments, cheque actions) refresh balances, invoices and reports with `useInvalidateFinance()`
  from `features/finance/finance-components`.
- CRM screens (`features/crm`) share badges, member / currency options and `ReasonDialog` from `crm-components`;
  opportunity stage changes go through `useOpportunityActions()` and activity toggles through `useActivityActions()`
  so the board, summary and dashboard caches stay in sync. A quote started from an opportunity opens
  `/sales/quotes/new?partnerId=…&opportunityId=…`.
- Expense screens (`features/expenses`) are self-service first: `/expenses/my` and the form need no permission,
  the API scopes reports to the owner. Action buttons follow the `can*` flags of the report detail; after any
  mutation call `useInvalidateExpenses()` (expense, treasury and workflow caches). Receipts upload through
  `useExpenseReportsUploadReceipt` before the report is saved.
- Project screens (`features/projects`) need no permission for members: `/projects/my-tasks` and
  `/projects/timesheet` are self-service, the detail page follows `canManage`, `canSeeCosts`, `isMember` and
  `canLogTime` from the API. The task board moves cards optimistically and calls `useInvalidateProjects()`
  (project, time entry and expense caches) after every mutation.
- Payroll screens (`features/payroll`): `/payroll/my` and `/payroll/payslips/$id` need no permission (the API
  only returns the caller's approved payslips); the rest need `payroll:read` (`/payroll/settings`:
  `payroll:update`). Period actions follow the `can*` flags of the period detail; after any mutation call
  `useInvalidatePayroll()` (payroll, salary and treasury caches). `SalaryHistory` is shared by the salaries
  page and the employee detail tab.
- Recruitment screens (`features/recruitment`): `/recruitment/interviews` needs no permission (the API only
  returns the caller's interviews); the rest need `recruitment:read`, actions follow `recruitment:create`,
  `update`, `delete` and `hire`. After any mutation call `useInvalidateRecruitment()` (posting, candidate,
  application, interview and offer caches). The application board uses native drag and drop and sends the
  target stage and position.
- Performance and training screens (`features/performance`, `features/training`): `/performance/my`,
  `/performance/reviews/$id` and `/training/my` need no permission (the API scopes the data); the rest need
  `performance:read` or `training:read`. The review page renders from the API flags (`canSelfReview`,
  `canManagerReview`, `canReturn`, …) and keeps unsaved ratings as overrides until saved. After mutations
  call `useInvalidatePerformance()` or `useInvalidateTraining()`.
- Support screens (`features/support`): `/support/my` and `/support/tickets/$id` need no permission (the API
  returns 404 for tickets the user may not see); `/support` needs `support:read` and `/support/settings`
  `support:update`. The ticket page renders from the API flags (`canManage`, `canComment`, `canClose`,
  `canReopen`, `canRate`, `nextStatuses`). After mutations call `useInvalidateSupport()`.
- Contract screens (`features/contracts`): `/contracts` needs `contracts:read`, `/contracts/types`
  `contracts:update`; `/contracts/$id` needs no permission (the API returns 404 unless the user holds
  `contracts:read` or owns the contract). The page renders from the API flags (`canEdit`, `canActivate`,
  `canRenew`, `canTerminate`, `canCancelTermination`, `canDelete`). `PartyContracts` embeds the list on
  partner and employee pages. After mutations call `useInvalidateContracts()`.
- Budget screens (`features/budgets`): `/budgets` (optional `?year`) and `/budgets/$id` need no
  permission (the API lists only owned budgets without `budgets:read` and returns 404 otherwise);
  `/budgets/entries` needs `budgets:read`, `/budgets/items` `budgets:update`. The page renders from the
  API flags (`canUpdate`, `canEdit`, `canApprove`, `canReopen`, `canDelete`); the plan grid is editable
  only with `canEdit`. `DocumentLink` opens the source document of an actual when the user may read
  it. After mutations call `useInvalidateBudgets()`.
- Fleet screens (`features/fleet`): `/fleet` and `/fleet/fuel` need `fleet:read`; `/fleet/$id` needs no
  permission (the API returns 404 unless the user reads the fleet or drives the vehicle) and renders from
  `canManage`, `isDriver` and `canDelete`; `/fleet/my` lists the user's own vehicles. `FuelDialog` and
  `ReadingDialog` serve both managers and drivers. After mutations call `useInvalidateFleet()`.
- Accounting screens (`features/accounting`): read pages need `accounting:read`, `/accounting/journal/new`
  and `/accounting/journal/edit/$id` need `accounting:update`. The entry page renders from the API flags
  (`canEdit`, `canPost`, `canReverse`, `canDelete`); `SourceDocumentLink` opens the source document
  (`documentId`) when the user may read it. Long lists (accounts, partners) use `OptionPicker`. Ledger,
  trial balance, balance sheet and income statement keep their filters in the URL. After mutations call
  `useInvalidateAccounting()`.
- e-Invoice screens (`features/einvoice`): `/e-invoices` (search `direction`) and `/e-invoices/$id` need
  `einvoice:read`; actions follow the API flags (`canResend`, `canRecord`, `canRespond`) and
  `einvoice:send|update`. Pages poll while a record is in flight (`IN_FLIGHT` in `einvoice-rules.ts`).
  The sales invoice detail hides cancel when `blocksSalesCancel` is true. After mutations call
  `useInvalidateEInvoices()`.
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by the router plugin on `pnpm dev`/`pnpm build`; commit it.

## Commands

| Task | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Dev server (proxies `/api` → :3000) | `pnpm dev` |
| Regenerate API client (API must run) | `pnpm api:generate` |
| Type check / lint / format | `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format` |
| Unit tests / E2E | `pnpm test`, `pnpm e2e` |
